# patches/series — canonical apply-order manifest for the port patch stack.
# Created 2026-08-05 (audit rec: reports/audit-20260805.md, MINOR "no machine-readable
# patch apply-order manifest — reproducibility-from-patches depends on unrecorded ordering").
#
# PURPOSE
#   One patch filename per line, in the order they apply onto a clean pinned upstream
#   checkout (Blender 5.2 LTS @ fbe6228777e7, see upstream/PIN). Order is LEXICAL by
#   filename EXCEPT where a recorded fact forces a deviation; every deviation is called
#   out below with its evidence source (file:line or commit hash). Comment lines (`#`)
#   and blank lines are ignored by any consumer.
#
# CONTRACT (what the harness actually enforces vs what this file is for)
#   The harness does NOT clean-pin replay. harness/run.sh:118-140 runs a per-patch
#   TRI-STATE check against the LIVE upstream working tree: each patches/0*.patch must
#   either apply clean (pristine), reverse-apply clean (already applied), or be
#   "in-development" (its target files are being actively extended by an in-flight lane).
#   A true conflict is a patch failing both ways while touching files nobody has modified.
#   That check is order-independent, so this manifest is NOT required by the harness and
#   its absence was NOT a contract violation. This file exists for the OTHER reproducibility
#   path: replaying patches/ onto a fresh clean pin (`git apply` in listed order), needed by
#   any milestone that rebuilds the port from patches rather than from the live tree.
#
# VERIFICATION CAVEAT
#   The ordering here is reconstructed from recorded facts (progress.txt / fix_plan.md /
#   notes), each cited at its deviation. Full clean-pin replay verification (fresh upstream
#   clone, apply the whole series in order, diff against the live tree) is DISK-HEAVY
#   (multi-GB checkout) and is DEFERRED to the M3-boundary reconcile. It was intentionally
#   NOT performed when this manifest was written — no upstream clone, no apply/revert.
#
# DEVIATIONS FROM LEXICAL ORDER (2 patches relocated; 1 deviation region)
#   * 0016b and 0016c are moved OUT of their lexical slot (which would be between 0016 and
#     0017) to AFTER 0021. Reason: 0016b's source/blender/gpu/CMakeLists.txt hunk appends
#     wgpu_texture.{cc,hh} to the SRC list and its hunk context depends on the lane-A
#     shader-chain source lines (wgpu_shader_compiler.{cc,hh}) that patch 0019 adds — so
#     0016b only applies once 0019/0021 are present, "despite the 0016b name."
#       evidence: ledger/progress.txt:137 ("patch 0016b applies AFTER 0019/0021 despite
#                 name — driver reconciles numbering");
#                 notes/gpu-laneB-integration.md:143-144 ("effective apply-order is AFTER
#                 0019/0021 despite the 0016b").
#   * 0016c stacks on 0016b (both append to the same gpu/CMakeLists.txt SRC list; 0016c's
#     entries follow 0016b's), so it applies immediately after 0016b — i.e. also after 0021.
#       evidence: ledger/progress.txt:153 ("cumulative: 0016c on 0016b on lane-A tree").
#
# SAME-FILE STACKS (already satisfied by lexical order — recorded here so a replayer keeps
# them in order and does not "tidy" the numbers; NOT counted as deviations)
#   * 0081 < 0082 < 0083 share hunks in the same files; reverse-apply verified in order
#     0083->0082->0081 (individual reverse of 0081 alone fails, benign).
#       evidence: fix_plan.md:413-415; ledger/progress.txt:241.
#   * wgpu_shader.cc stack: 0084 < 0086 < 0087 < 0088 < 0090 (each stacks on the prior).
#       evidence: fix_plan.md:446; ledger/progress.txt:246-249, 255, 257.
#   * wgpu_vertex_buffer.cc stack: 0085 < 0091.
#       evidence: fix_plan.md:446; ledger/progress.txt:257.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

